{"id":"rdb-4dd186","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-c3b87a02-8353-4e1b-b8b4-06d63af37c0b","text":"## Implementation complete\n\n### Changes\n\n**`engine/catalog.go`** — 10 edits:\n\n1. **`tableState`**: Added `checks []sql.CheckDefinition` field\n2. **`cachedTableMeta`**: Added `checks` field so metadata cache preserves checks across transactions\n3. **`StartTransaction` cache hit path**: Threads checks through to new `tableState`\n4. **`StartTransaction` cache miss path**: Stores checks in cache\n5. **`checkDisk` struct**: New serialization type (name, expression, enforced)\n6. **`schemaDisk`**: Added `Checks []checkDisk` field (`omitempty` for backward compat)\n7. **`encodeSchema`**: New signature `(schema, checks)` — serializes check definitions\n8. **`decodeSchema`**: New return value `(schema, checks, error)` — deserializes checks\n9. **`loadTableMetadata`**: Stores decoded checks on tableState\n10. **Three commit paths**: Pass `state.checks` to `encodeSchema`\n\n**New methods on `table`**:\n- `GetChecks` — returns stored check definitions (implements `sql.CheckTable`)\n- `CreateCheck` — appends a check definition, marks dirty (implements `sql.CheckAlterableTable`)\n- `DropCheck` — removes a check by name, marks dirty\n\n**Interface assertions**: `sql.CheckTable`, `sql.CheckAlterableTable`\n\n**`engine/merge.go`** — 2 edits: Updated `decodeSchema` call sites to handle the new return value (checks are passed through but not actively merged — the schema blob contains them).\n\n**`engine/engine_test.go`** — 10 new tests:\n\n| Test | Coverage |\n|------|----------|\n| `TestCheckConstraintOnCreateTable` | Unnamed CHECK on CREATE TABLE, INSERT violation |\n| `TestCheckConstraintNamed` | Named CONSTRAINT on CREATE TABLE |\n| `TestCheckConstraintOnUpdate` | CHECK enforced on UPDATE |\n| `TestAlterTableAddCheck` | ALTER TABLE ADD CONSTRAINT ... CHECK |\n| `TestAlterTableAddCheckRejectsExistingViolations` | Rejects if existing rows violate |\n| `TestAlterTableDropCheck` | DROP CHECK removes enforcement |\n| `TestCheckConstraintPersistsThroughReopen` | Working-state persistence round-trip |\n| `TestCheckConstraintPersistsNativeGit` | Native git persistence round-trip |\n| `TestShowCreateTableIncludesCheck` | SHOW CREATE TABLE includes CHECK clause |\n| `TestNotNullOnNonPKColumn` | NOT NULL enforcement on non-PK columns |\n\n### Key finding during implementation\n\nThe metadata cache (`cachedTableMeta`) needed to include checks. Without this, checks were lost when a new auto-commit transaction started after the one that created the table — the cache hit path would reconstruct `tableState` without checks, causing DROP CHECK and INSERT enforcement to fail in the same session.\n\n### All tests pass\n\nFull suite: `go test ./...` — all packages green."},"created_at":"2026-09-14T10:19:01.223013Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.270 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
