{"id":"rdb-738fd0","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-a75ef1d4-eea0-44f6-bd6b-366b808bdc90","text":"Implementation complete. One method added to the prolly tree, plus 7 tests.\n\n**`tree.go`:**\n- `Tree.IteratorFrom(ctx, startKey)` — returns an `*Iterator` positioned at the first entry \u003e= `startKey`\n- `Iterator.seekTo(hash, startKey)` — internal method that navigates the B-tree using binary search at each level (same O(log N) descent as `Get`), then positions the iterator at the correct leaf entry. If the target key falls past the end of a leaf, it falls through to `advance()` to find the next leaf.\n\n**`tree_test.go` — 7 new tests:**\n1. `TestIteratorFromExactKey` — seek to an existing key\n2. `TestIteratorFromBetweenKeys` — seek between keys returns next entry\n3. `TestIteratorFromPastEnd` — seek past all keys returns done\n4. `TestIteratorFromEmptyStart` — nil start key returns first entry\n5. `TestIteratorFromSingleEntry` — single-entry tree\n6. `TestIteratorFromWalksRemainingEntries` — seek then iterate all remaining entries in order\n7. `TestIteratorFromPrefixScanPattern` — prefix scan pattern: seek to prefix, iterate while prefix matches\n\nFull suite passes."},"created_at":"2026-09-16T12:49:18.028882Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.273 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
