{"id":"rdb-01bfe4","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Update README to reflect shipped features","description":"The README has several outdated claims that contradict recently shipped work:\n\n1. **\"Secondary indexes … are not yet supported\"** — non-unique secondary indexes (`rdb-4bdf5d`) and UNIQUE constraints (`rdb-a1f9d1`) have shipped.\n2. **\"`ALTER TABLE` [is] not yet supported\"** — ALTER TABLE landed in `e8c896c`.\n3. **Roadmap** — M6 items (secondary indexes, broader SQL compatibility) are partially complete; the checklist should reflect progress.\n4. **No mention of new types/constraints** — ENUM, DECIMAL/NUMERIC, JSON, DATE/TIME/DATETIME/TIMESTAMP, CHECK constraints, DEFAULT values, and collation-aware comparisons have all shipped but are absent from the README.\n\n### Changes needed\n\n- Update the \"current SQL scope\" paragraph (around line 197) to reflect what is now supported.\n- Update the roadmap checklist to reflect M5/M6 progress.\n- Optionally mention expanded type and constraint support in the feature summary.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"a0","labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-16T20:18:13.420956Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.273 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
