{"id":"rdb-01bfe4","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6c57e60c-3b6c-4eea-b87c-a43169769429","text":"Updated two sections of README.md:\n\n1. **SQL scope paragraph** — replaced the outdated \"not yet supported\" list with an accurate summary of current capabilities: ALTER TABLE, secondary indexes (unique/non-unique), CHECK/DEFAULT, collation, and all shipped types. Only auto-increment and foreign keys remain listed as unsupported.\n\n2. **Roadmap** — split M6 into completed (partial) and remaining items so readers can see what's shipped vs. what's ahead.\n\nNo other sections changed — quickstart, embedded API, architecture, performance, and installation are still accurate."},"created_at":"2026-09-16T20:19:10.318592Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.273 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
