{"id":"rdb-33512b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a0","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-17T10:19:45.171013Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.273 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-33512b","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-9d3c8465-9bf5-4ffd-948f-55d2a9c5960d","text":"Created `docs/guide.md` (~420 lines) covering the full operational lifecycle:\n\n1. **Setup** — `init`, repo structure, `refs/repodb/data`\n2. **Starting the server** — `start` flags, MySQL client access\n3. **Persistence modes** — journal vs native-git, how to switch, checkpointing, mixed-mode guard\n4. **Data lifecycle** — `status`, `diff`, `commit`\n5. **CLI reference** — all 11 commands with complete flag tables\n6. **Synchronization** — `enable`, `sync`, tracking refs, the fetch/merge/push cycle\n7. **Conflict resolution** — `conflicts`, `resolve`, resolution choices, distributed identity guidance\n8. **Embedded Go API** — open/session pattern, snapshot isolation, recovery\n9. **Backup and recovery** — what to copy, cache is disposable, worktree sharing, legacy import\n10. **Git interaction** — what git commands do/don't do, locking, integrity checks\n\nAlso added a row to the README documentation table linking to the guide."},"created_at":"2026-09-17T10:21:41.72167Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.273 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-3c8ef9","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Currently `repodb sync` refuses to run if the journal has uncheckpointed changes, requiring the user to manually run `repodb commit -m '...'` first.\n\nImprove the UX by detecting the dirty journal and offering to checkpoint automatically before proceeding with sync. If running non-interactively (no TTY), keep the current error behavior.\n\nThis avoids a confusing error for users who don't yet understand the checkpoint/sync relationship.","estimate":2,"labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aG","status":"BACKLOG","title":"repodb sync: prompt to checkpoint when journal is dirty"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T13:20:42.312469Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.273 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-bc2820","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"`repodb enable --remote origin` saves `repodb.remote=origin` to Git config, but `sync`, `conflicts`, and `resolve` never read it back — they all require `--remote` on every invocation via `requireRemote()`.\n\nWhen `--remote` is omitted, these commands should fall back to the saved `repodb.remote` config value. This eliminates repetitive flag passing after the one-time `enable` setup.\n\nAffected commands: `sync`, `conflicts`, `resolve`. The `enable` command itself should continue to require an explicit `--remote` since it's the one that sets the config.","estimate":2,"labels":["feature"],"sort_order":"aH","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Default --remote flag to saved repodb.remote config"},"created_at":"2026-09-17T13:30:55.857396Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.273 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
