{"id":"rdb-1ced7f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-0d5c7545-4ea0-4682-a17e-fdb5ec9a1d47","text":"Implementation complete. All 14 test packages pass.\n\n**Changes in `engine/catalog.go`:**\n- Added `rekeyAllRows` method on `tableState` — re-encodes all row keys using the current schema, detects duplicate keys, builds combined delete-old + insert-new edits, and invalidates all index manifest entries to force full rebuild on commit\n- Modified `DropColumn` — replaced blanket PK rejection with: reject only if it's the sole PK column; for composite PKs, remove the ordinal from PkOrdinals and call `rekeyAllRows` after cell removal\n- Modified `ModifyColumn` — removed PK type-change rejection guard; after existing type conversion and optional reorder, calls `rekeyAllRows` when a PK column's type changed\n\n**Changes in `engine/engine_test.go`:**\n- Updated `TestAlterTableModifyPKTypeRejected` → `TestAlterTableModifyPKColumnType` (verifies BIGINT→TEXT re-keying works)\n- Updated `TestAlterTableModifyPKLengthRejected` → `TestAlterTableModifyPKColumnLength` (verifies VARCHAR(100)→VARCHAR(50) re-keying works)\n- 10 new tests:\n  - `DropPKColumnComposite` — composite PK drop with PK uniqueness verification\n  - `DropPKColumnDuplicateRejected` — collision detection on composite PK drop\n  - `DropPKColumnWithIndex` — secondary index rebuilt after PK column drop\n  - `DropPKColumnPersistsJournal` / `DropPKColumnPersistsNativeGit` — persistence\n  - `ModifyPKColumnTypeDuplicateRejected` — VARCHAR→BIGINT collision detection\n  - `ModifyPKColumnTypeWithIndex` — secondary index rebuilt after PK type change\n  - `ModifyPKColumnTypePersistsJournal` / `ModifyPKColumnTypePersistsNativeGit` — persistence\n  - `ModifyPKColumnTypeComposite` — composite PK, change one column's type\n\nNo decisions outside the spec."},"created_at":"2026-09-18T08:07:56.860438Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.275 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-1ced7f","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-57b77e08-18b4-4ce8-be2d-ef57192617d9","text":"Addressed two correctness issues from review:\n\n**Fix 1: Pending deletes lost during re-keying**\nReplaced `rekeyAllRows` (mutating method on `tableState`) with `rekeyRows` (standalone function). The new function preserves delete edits from `oldEdits` in the output, so rows deleted earlier in an explicit transaction remain deleted after re-keying.\n\n**Fix 2: Failed re-keying leaves partially mutated state**\n- `DropColumn` (PK path): builds candidate schema, candidate rows, and calls `rekeyRows` to validate — all as local variables. Only installs into `t.state` after validation succeeds.\n- `ModifyColumn` (PK type change): adds a pre-mutation validation pass — builds candidate rows (cloned + converted) and candidate schema, calls `rekeyRows`. If duplicates are detected, returns error before any state mutation. The actual re-keying at the end of the method (after schema/row/reorder mutations) is guaranteed to succeed since we already validated the same PK values.\n\n**New tests:**\n- `DropPKColumnPreservesTransactionDeletes` — explicit transaction: DELETE then DROP PK column, verify delete survives\n- `ModifyPKTypePreservesTransactionDeletes` — explicit transaction: DELETE then MODIFY PK type, verify delete survives\n- `DropPKColumnDuplicateDoesNotCorruptState` — failed DROP leaves table queryable with original schema\n- `ModifyPKTypeDuplicateDoesNotCorruptState` — failed MODIFY leaves table queryable with original types\n\nAll 14 test packages pass."},"created_at":"2026-09-18T09:14:52.508824Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.275 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
