{"id":"rdb-ef8c25","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-d76ba2de-8343-49c3-859c-d27c144e5e62","text":"Implementation ready for review.\n\n**Change:** `Makefile` has a new `cross-windows` target (`GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64` `go build ./...` + `go vet ./...`). `test` depends on it, so the cross-compile runs before `go test ./...`. The target is also in `.PHONY`.\n\n**Verification**\n- `make test` passes on the current tree: both Windows steps succeed, then the full suite passes.\n- Non-test code check: a temporary Unix-only reference (`unix.LOCK_EX`) in a non-test file makes `go build` fail and `make` exit 2.\n- Test code check: the same reference in a `_test.go` file is caught by `go vet`. `make test` exits 2 before `go test` runs.\n- Both temporary files were removed; the only change is the Makefile."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T07:14:22.80486Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
