{"id":"rdb-1e11b2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2ebd0a51-2978-453d-adfd-0f4516fd9dbb","text":"Implemented per spec.\n\n- `common/git/git.go`: `PushRef` and `PushCommit` now pass `--no-verify`. These were the only production push call sites (others are tests and the `experiments/gitstorage` prototype).\n- `common/git/git_test.go` (new): `TestDataPushesSkipPrePushHook` — local repo + bare remote, pre-push hook that writes a marker and exits 1. Asserts both pushes succeed, the remote ref advances to each commit, and the marker is never written. Confirmed it fails without the fix (hook rejects `PushRef`) and passes with it.\n- `make test` passes, including the Windows cross-compile and vet.\n\nNo decisions beyond the spec. Server-side hooks still run, since `--no-verify` only skips the client-side `pre-push` hook."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T07:56:06.929946Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
