{"id":"rdb-855cac","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Upgrade go-mysql-server to latest main (Go 1.26, gms_pure_go)","description":"RepoDB pins `github.com/dolthub/go-mysql-server v0.20.0` (May 2025, the latest tag). It pulls in old indirect deps that govulncheck flags (grpc v1.53.0, protobuf v1.28.1, x/text v0.6.0, logrus v1.8.1). RepoDB doesn't reach the vulnerable code, but staying pinned to a 16-month-old GMS isn't sustainable.\n\nLatest GMS `main` (`v0.20.1-0.20260925233942-d8e4c765db15`) bumps grpc 1.79.3, protobuf 1.36.10, x/text 0.37.0, logrus 1.8.3. Consequences:\n\n- **Go 1.26.2** floor (approved).\n- **API breaks**: ~25 compile errors in `engine/` — `*sql.Context` added to `Schema`/`PrimaryKeySchema`/`ColumnExpressionTypes`/expression methods, `types.JsonToMySqlString` and `CreateFunc1Args` signatures, `sql.ConvertInRange` no longer a bool.\n- **Regex backend**: since 2025-09 go-icu-regex needs cgo + ICU4C. Decision: build with `-tags gms_pure_go` (Go regexp) to keep RepoDB free of C dependencies; document that consumers must pass the tag.\n\n- [ ] Bump GMS (+ vitess etc.) and go directive\n- [ ] Fix API breaks in engine/\n- [ ] Makefile builds/tests/vets with `gms_pure_go` (incl. Windows cross-compile)\n- [ ] README: Go 1.26, build tag requirement\n- [ ] Full test suite + govulncheck","status":"PLANNED","estimate":3,"sort_order":"a0","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-855cac","target_id":"rdb-d3c729","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-28T09:26:35.700209Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
