{"id":"rdb-ec8ec2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6f14437c-22e0-4d91-bf3e-dcbf52e3fb7c","text":"Implemented per spec (the interim latest.md and the stray numbers in other docs were refined in the spec).\n\n- `docs/benchmarks/latest.md` is the canonical current-results file. Interim: it says no clean single-commit run exists yet, lists what changed since, and links the 2026-09-13 report; no copied tables.\n- `docs/benchmarks/history/`: five dated reports with banners (M2 baseline split out of sql-m2.md; M4 merge/sync; M4.2; M4.3 with the rdb-3745e6 caveat; M4.4 scorecard plus its 4 JSONs). All moved via `git mv`.\n- `docs/benchmark.md` is methodology only, plus a new \"Publishing results\" section (4-step process and banner template).\n- README: dated caption on the performance table, links to latest/methodology, `make bench` default corrected (native-git), docs table entry \"Benchmarks\".\n- Links updated in plan.md, guide.md, working-state.md, sql-m2.md.\n- Checks: link and anchor script over README + docs (17 files, 0 broken); every history file has its banner; `git diff --check`; `make lint`; `make test`.\n\nFresh measurement is tracked in rdb-6ae82d (blocked by rdb-bc42f6)."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T10:46:30.920048Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
