{"id":"rdb-802f5d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"dbbench aborts Git workloads when auto-gc removes objects during size measurement","description":"Found in the rdb-6ae82d run at `e33870e`. For every fixture size, the native-git scorecard stopped after `clone_enable_open`, so `sync_unchanged`, `edit_sync_roundtrip`, `divergent_edit_merge` and `conflict_resolve_roundtrip` were never measured:\n\n```\nFAILED: rows=1000: lstat …/1000/local/.git/objects/62/3a25bb…: no such file or directory\n```\n\n`directoryBytes` (fixture growth) walks the repositories with `filepath.WalkDir` while Git's background auto-gc (detached after fetch/push) prunes loose objects. A file vanishing between the directory read and the `lstat` returns an error that aborts the fixture. The 2026-09-13 native-git run hit the same thing: its `failure` field reads \"directory-size measurement: loose object removed by GC between snapshots\".\n\nFix: files or directories that disappear during the walk contribute 0 bytes instead of failing. Growth is documented as an approximate logical size.","status":"PLANNED","estimate":1,"sort_order":"a0","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-802f5d","target_id":"rdb-6ae82d","kind":"blocks"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-09-28T11:42:02.427068Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-802f5d","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"created"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T11:42:11.14542Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-802f5d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@macbook.local\u003e","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-28T11:42:11.169222Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-802f5d","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a1","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-28T11:42:13.349181Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-802f5d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-970c330e-b457-4b31-b764-ee4e4445a2b2","text":"Fixed per spec. `directoryBytes` skips `fs.ErrNotExist` from the walk, and a new `entryBytes` helper returns 0 for an entry that vanished between listing and stat. Other errors still fail. How the error propagates didn't need changing: with ENOENT tolerated, the remaining errors are real I/O failures.\n\nTest `TestEntryBytesToleratesVanishedFile` covers a file removed after `ReadDir` and a missing root. The native-git smoke run completes all four sync workloads. `make lint` and the dbbench tests pass."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T11:43:21.887951Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
