{"id":"rdb-6ae82d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-1f24ac24-a5e4-4443-a999-52b67c06c028","text":"First run at `e33870e` was aborted. Native-git stopped each fixture before its sync workloads because of a harness bug: auto-gc pruned objects during `directoryBytes`, filed and fixed as rdb-802f5d (`57a0cd8`). All four runs must share a revision, so the whole run restarts at `57a0cd8`. The partial output is kept in the scratchpad (`aborted-e33870e/`) and won't be published.\n\nA clean worktree and binary at `57a0cd8` are ready. The launch is on hold because unrelated containers (`agent-lang-shakedown` image, one at ~85% CPU) are running on the benchmark machine."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T11:43:48.236425Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-59c7d7","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Journal-mode merge sync ~2.3x slower than 2026-09-13 scorecard","description":"Measured in the rdb-6ae82d scorecard at `57a0cd8` vs the 2026-09-13 report (journal run at `c30d2ef`+dirty), 50k rows, p50:\n\n| Workload | 2026-09-13 | 2026-09-28 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Sync unchanged | 682 ms | 953 ms |\n| Edit/sync roundtrip | 2,491 ms | 3,807 ms |\n| Divergent merge | 8,541 ms | 19,818 ms |\n| Conflict resolve | 9,218 ms | 20,721 ms |\n\nNative-git sync did not regress in the same way (divergent merge 2,550 → 2,331 ms). Not yet investigated.\n\nCandidate explanations to check, not conclusions:\n- rdb-3745e6 made checkpoints materialize pending row edits. Journal sync checkpoints before exchanging history, so if the old run's sync path dropped or skipped row materialization, it was doing less work.\n- rdb-e472aa's index-edit derivation and cache.\n- rdb-bc42f6's per-read stat checks.\n- The GMS upgrade.\n\nApproach: phase counters (checkpoint vs fetch/merge/push) per iteration at both revisions, and bisect across the merged issues.","status":"BACKLOG","estimate":3,"sort_order":"aA","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-59c7d7","target_id":"rdb-6ae82d","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["task"]},"created_at":"2026-09-28T12:51:58.689261Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-59c7d7","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"description":"Measured in the rdb-6ae82d scorecard at `57a0cd8` vs the 2026-09-13 report, 50k rows, p50. The old journal run was at `c30d2ef` plus uncommitted changes: M4.4 work in progress, before the final M4.4 commit `864731d`.\n\n| Workload | 2026-09-13 | 2026-09-28 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Sync unchanged | 682 ms | 953 ms |\n| Edit/sync roundtrip | 2,491 ms | 3,807 ms |\n| Divergent merge | 8,541 ms | 19,818 ms |\n| Conflict resolve | 9,218 ms | 20,721 ms |\n\nNative-git sync did not regress in the same way (divergent merge 2,550 → 2,331 ms, though the old native-git run aborted its sync workloads partway; see rdb-802f5d). Not yet investigated.\n\nCandidate explanations to check, not conclusions:\n- The rest of M4.4 (`864731d`), since the old run predates its final form.\n- rdb-3745e6 made checkpoints materialize pending row edits. Journal sync checkpoints before exchanging history, so if the old sync path skipped row materialization, it was doing less work.\n- rdb-e472aa's index-edit derivation and cache.\n- rdb-bc42f6's per-read stat checks.\n- The GMS upgrade.\n\nApproach: phase counters (checkpoint vs fetch/merge/push) per iteration, then bisect `864731d` → `57a0cd8` with a reduced scorecard (`-rows 50000 -clients 1 -requests 5`, sync workloads only).","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-28T12:53:18.835295Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-6ae82d","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-63425975-a6bf-412a-bb78-732f82e6c2b1","text":"Full run completed at `57a0cd8`, 11:44–12:49 UTC. Native-git 14 min, journal 50 min, MySQL 10 s, Dolt 13 s. All four JSONs record `57a0cd8` with a clean tree, suite v1 and the default config. The external ones record `server_version` (8.4.11; Dolt 2.3.5).\n\n**Published**\n- `docs/benchmarks/latest.md`:\n  - environment, commands, wall times, summary;\n  - changes since 2026-09-13, stated without attribution: the old native-git run predates M4.4 and the old journal run was uncommitted M4.4 work;\n  - tables generated from the JSON; the concurrency table shows p50 / ops/s / rejected share;\n  - correctness failures (Dolt only), run metadata, reading notes (including the loopback-TCP caveat and RepoDB's own wire-protocol point read, 0.14 ms).\n- `docs/benchmarks/latest/*.json`.\n- README table and prose, verified programmatically against the JSON.\n\n**Findings**\n- MySQL, journal and native-git passed every correctness check.\n- Dolt 2.3.5 lost acknowledged increments at 1k rows (120→40, 480→34) and returned serialization errors at 10k/50k. Those errors stopped the fixtures before the 16-client rows, which the file marks \"not measured\".\n- Journal merge sync is ~2.3× slower than the old report: filed as rdb-59c7d7 (BACKLOG).\n\n**Deviation from spec**: the interim latest.md was replaced, not archived, as planned (it held no results).\n\nChecks: link check (17 files, 0 broken), `make lint`, `git diff --check`."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T12:54:05.569205Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
