{"id":"rdb-92b9e2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b04d5349-967e-4650-a53f-d406760af785","text":"Implemented; spec revised to match. A lazy base alone still produced 21 loads, so replay also defers applying transactions, which a later checkpoint supersedes.\n\n**Tests:** `TestJournalReplayLoadsBoundedSnapshots` (clean / dirty-tail / base-change) goes from 21–22 snapshot loads to ≤ 1. `make test`, race tests (repository/engine/integration/cmd) and `make lint` pass.\n\n**Probe** (journal, 1k rows, 10 syncs/workload, git-call wrapper):\n\n| Workload | before total (first→last) | after total (first→last) |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| sync_unchanged | 5.9 s (0.6→0.6) | 4.6 s (0.4→0.4) |\n| edit_sync_roundtrip | 20.1 s (1.5→2.5) | 15.2 s (1.5→1.5) |\n| divergent_edit_merge | 65.3 s (3.3→9.6) | 31.8 s (3.4→2.9) |\n| conflict_resolve_roundtrip | 80.0 s (3.9→12.6) | 44.0 s (3.8→3.9) |\n\n- Distinct ls-tree commits per push, before: 2,4,4,6…22; after: 3,4,3,4…\n- Git calls per push, before: 47→408; after: flat 58/84.\n\nThe 30-sync scorecard gain should be larger; it will be measured at the next latest.md refresh. What remains is a flat ~3–4 s per journal merge sync at 1k rows (native-git ~1.3–1.5 s), which is rdb-2c93ca's territory."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T13:14:22.366516Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-59c7d7","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-b6a8c2b3-8c1e-4fd9-a920-3f992330707a","text":"Likely explained by rdb-92b9e2: cold journal replay loaded a snapshot for every historical checkpoint, so journal sync cost grew with history (quadratic over the scorecard's 30 syncs). With that fix, per-sync cost is flat in a 10-sync probe. Confirm or close this issue after the next full scorecard refresh."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T13:14:22.39502Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-92b9e2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-86c8e80d-f803-45cb-a69b-9a3e1fe5f679","text":"Review fix: `TestJournalReplayLoadsBoundedSnapshots` allowed 2 snapshot loads in the `base-change` case, while the spec and handoff claim ≤ 1 for every case, so a regression adding a second load would have passed. The per-case `maxLoads` field is removed and all three cases assert ≤ 1 (the measured value). They pass, and `make lint` passes. No production-code change."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T13:24:21.31764Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
