{"id":"rdb-6bf1cc","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-fbcec595-c330-448b-b331-abe5e630f0d7","text":"Implemented per spec.\n\n**Root cause** (upstream go-mysql-server): the tabular EXPLAIN is a placeholder row with the string \"NULL\" in every column, including the NOT NULL `Uint64` `rows` column, so wire encoding fails. It affected every MySQL client, not just the CLI; embedded use only ever got the placeholder.\n\n**Fix**\n- `engine.NormalizeExplain` rewrites a plain EXPLAIN/DESCRIBE/DESC of a statement to EXPLAIN PLAN. It is parser-checked: `DESCRIBE \u003ctable\u003e`, `EXPLAIN PLAN`, `FORMAT=` and `ANALYZE` stay unchanged. A cheap leading-keyword check means other queries are never parsed twice.\n- Applied in `Session.Query` (all embedded paths) and by a new `explainInterceptor` registered on the MySQL server (`Query`/`MultiQuery`; prepared statements pass through).\n\n**Tests**\n- `TestNormalizeExplain` (17 cases).\n- `TestPlainExplainReturnsPlan` (embedded).\n- `TestMySQLWireRoundTrip`: EXPLAIN plus DESCRIBE over the wire. Without the interceptor it fails with the original ParseUint error.\n\n**End to end:** `repodb sql 'EXPLAIN …'` prints the plan; `DESCRIBE t` prints columns. `make test`, `make lint` and `git diff --check` pass."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:27:46.025109Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
