{"id":"rdb-d86f52","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ba02895e-cbc3-44ea-a87c-b301409dff09","text":"Implemented per spec. Four passages were updated. The issue listed three; `docs/guide.md`'s Git interaction section had a fourth.\n\n- **README Installation:** \"requires POSIX file locking\" is replaced with the exact platform status: macOS + Git 2.55 is the tested baseline; Windows builds and passes `go vet` on every `make test`, but the suite has not been run on Windows.\n- **guide.md:** the publish lock is \"a file lock (`flock(2)` on Unix, `LockFileEx` on Windows)\", shared across worktrees and processes.\n- **storage-format.md, lock description:** the lock goes through `gofrs/flock`, advisory on Unix and mandatory on Windows. That doesn't matter because lock files are only held; `working.lock` works the same way.\n- **storage-format.md, qualification:** the \"requires POSIX `flock`\" sentence is replaced with the Windows/Linux qualification status.\n\nThe Windows status is taken from the rdb-6e40a9 walkthrough: the Windows code is compile- and vet-checked only.\n\n`grep -i posix` over README and docs finds nothing outside `plan.md`. The link check and `git diff --check` pass."},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:29:33.207863Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.283 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
