{"id":"rdb-515fae","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"parent_id":"rdb-19616b","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:10.066985Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-4a685e","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"parent_id":"rdb-19616b","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:10.114457Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-7b1006","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Introduce one canonical snapshot selector accepted by repository, engine, embedded, and CLI read paths.\n\nSelectors must support full commit IDs, unambiguous prefixes, and named data refs without changing the live data head. Invalid, ambiguous, unreachable, or incompatible snapshots return classified errors. This is the foundation for log, diff, historical queries, restore, and revert.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-3a56dc","sort_order":"aF","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Address immutable data snapshots across CLI and embedded APIs"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:53.665953Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-ce14fb","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add read-only history inspection, including a `repodb log` command and embedded API.\n\nShow snapshot ID, parents, timestamp, author/committer, checkpoint message, format version, and available table/schema summary. Support bounded pagination and machine-readable output. History inspection must not materialize or mutate working state.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-3a56dc","sort_order":"aG","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Inspect data history and snapshot metadata"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:53.694926Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-71f167","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Allow SQL reads against an explicitly selected historical snapshot without moving the live head.\n\nProvide an embedded API and CLI surface such as `repodb sql --at \u003csnapshot\u003e ...`; evaluate a SQL-level `AS OF` form separately in the spec. Historical sessions are read-only, pinned for their lifetime, and report clear errors for writes, incompatible formats, or missing objects.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-3a56dc","sort_order":"aH","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Query an immutable historical snapshot"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:53.726244Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-493758","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Compare any two snapshots—or working state against a snapshot—and report schema plus row-level changes.\n\nOutput must identify table, primary key, change kind, and before/after values, support table filtering and machine-readable output, and stream or bound memory for large diffs. Existing table-level `repodb diff` behavior must remain compatible or receive an explicit migration path.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-3a56dc","sort_order":"aI","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Diff rows and schemas between data snapshots"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:53.765379Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-33692c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Represent independent named data histories as dedicated RepoDB refs without coupling them to source-code branches.\n\nSupport create, list, rename, and delete operations with validated names, immutable starting points, safe default-branch behavior, and explicit remote tracking rules. Deletion must refuse when it would strand unmerged history unless forced through an auditable operation.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-3a56dc","sort_order":"aJ","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Create and manage named data branches"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:53.798808Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-23dce8","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add branch-aware working state and a safe `repodb switch` workflow.\n\nEach data branch must have isolated journal/conflict state. Switching with uncheckpointed changes must preserve them on the originating branch or refuse with clear recovery instructions—never reset implicitly. Embedded/server sessions pinned before a switch must have defined behavior, and linked Git worktrees must not accidentally share the wrong data branch.","estimate":8,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-3a56dc","sort_order":"aK","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Switch data branches without losing working changes"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:53.83175Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-e35ef0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Expose explicit local data-branch merging using RepoDB’s three-way row/schema merge engine.\n\nSupport fast-forward and two-parent merge commits, preserve both histories, reuse durable conflict inspection/resolution, validate constraints before publication, and never alter source-code branches. Define behavior when either branch has dirty working state.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-3a56dc","sort_order":"aL","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Merge named data branches"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:53.870294Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-a2b302","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Restore selected tables or rows from a historical snapshot into the current working transaction.\n\nThe operation creates ordinary pending changes that can be inspected before checkpointing; it does not move refs or erase later history. Support dry-run/diff output, dependency validation, missing-row/table behavior, and atomic failure.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-3a56dc","sort_order":"aM","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Restore selected tables or rows from a snapshot"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:53.91166Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-9bbd62","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Create a new data commit that reverses a selected earlier commit while preserving subsequent history.\n\nCompute the inverse relative to the target commit’s parent, apply it through normal merge/conflict and constraint machinery, provide a preview, and refuse ambiguous merge-commit reverts until a mainline parent is chosen. Never implement revert by moving the live ref backward.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-3a56dc","sort_order":"aN","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Revert a committed data change"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:53.946322Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-8d63a3","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Add authorization after connection authentication.\n\nSupport users/roles and least-privilege grants for database, table, and administrative operations; enforce them consistently for direct SQL, prepared statements, metadata queries, and maintenance commands exposed through the server. Credential and privilege changes must be durable without leaking secrets into normal data history. Include an explicit bootstrap/recovery path for administrators.","estimate":8,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-04786e","sort_order":"aO","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Enforce database roles and privileges"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:53.980045Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-d0b39d","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Define a stable server configuration surface for bind addresses, TLS, credentials, limits, logging, and repository selection.\n\nSupport config file, environment/secret injection, and CLI override precedence; reject unsafe file permissions or secret placement where practical. Provide a production profile with secure defaults and an explicit local-development profile. Startup diagnostics must explain why configuration is rejected without printing secrets.","estimate":3,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-04786e","sort_order":"aP","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Provide secure server configuration and secret handling"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:54.009222Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-df7bec","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Make a long-running standalone server diagnosable and bounded.\n\nExpose structured logs and metrics for connections, queries, transaction outcomes, conflicts, checkpoints, sync, latency, and storage growth. Add configurable connection/query limits, idle and statement timeouts, graceful shutdown, and health/readiness signals. Ensure telemetry excludes credentials and sensitive row values by default.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-04786e","sort_order":"aQ","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Add server observability and resource controls"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:54.046445Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-65b203","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Implement the INFORMATION_SCHEMA and MySQL metadata behavior needed by the supported driver/ORM profile.\n\nCover table, column, index, constraint, generated-key, and foreign-key metadata; preserve stable type and error reporting through prepared statements. Scope is driven by the compatibility test suite rather than an unbounded promise of complete MySQL metadata compatibility.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-864fc6","sort_order":"aR","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Expose compatible schema metadata for drivers and ORMs"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:54.079958Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-8b1539","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Turn compatibility from anecdote into a versioned release contract.\n\nDefine supported versions and CRUD/migration scenarios for selected MySQL drivers and ORMs, run the profile in CI through the wire server, publish known limitations, and prevent regressions. The profile should include generated keys, transactions, prepared statements, schema discovery, constraints, and representative migrations.","estimate":3,"labels":["task"],"parent_id":"rdb-864fc6","sort_order":"aS","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Publish and enforce an application compatibility profile"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:54.114632Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-f33cb0","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Back up all authoritative state needed to recover committed history and acknowledged journal work while embedded or server workloads are active.\n\nDefine a consistent backup boundary, produce a portable artifact or documented repository layout, verify checksums/format, and provide a restore command that validates before publication. Add round-trip, interrupted-backup, dirty-journal, and remote-independent recovery tests.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-19616b","sort_order":"aT","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Create consistent online backup and verified restore"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:54.145753Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-92cd4a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Provide explicit, crash-safe upgrades between persisted RepoDB formats.\n\nDetect old/new/unsupported formats before mutation; plan and execute idempotent migrations with backup/rollback guidance; preserve commit history where possible; and test old-binary/new-binary compatibility boundaries. Never partially advance the live ref or journal authority on migration failure.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-19616b","sort_order":"aU","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Add storage-format migration and compatibility framework"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:54.18635Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-93382e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Define safe repository maintenance for long-lived data histories and branches.\n\nReport storage by live snapshots, journals, branches, tracking refs, conflicts, and unreachable objects. Add retention/pruning policies that protect branch tips, remote tracking state, active readers, dirty journals, backups, and recovery windows before delegating object cleanup to Git. Provide dry-run and auditable results.","estimate":5,"labels":["feature"],"parent_id":"rdb-19616b","sort_order":"aV","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Manage Git history retention and unreachable data objects"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:54.218341Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-0a5b56","type":"CREATE","payload":{"description":"Publish and continuously verify the supported standalone-server operating envelope.\n\nRun a multi-day soak and fault suite covering restart, concurrent clients, checkpoint/sync, backup/restore, certificate rotation, credential changes, storage growth, resource limits, and version upgrades. Document supported topology, workload limits, secure configuration, recovery objectives, and known exclusions.","estimate":3,"labels":["task"],"parent_id":"rdb-19616b","sort_order":"aW","status":"BACKLOG","title":"Certify the standalone deployment profile"},"created_at":"2026-09-28T15:45:54.248208Z","created_by":"codex-mcp-client/0.158.0 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
