{"id":"rdb-53214c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-7b989230-9189-4e4e-956c-753a98f8c606","text":"Ready for review.\n\n**Fix:** in `WorkingState.Diff` (`common/repository/working.go`), a table whose manifest entries are equal is now skipped only if it has no pending journal row edits. Because `Diff` already walks the union of base and working tables, and pending tables are always in the working manifest, this single condition gives `modified` for existing tables and `added` for new ones without double listing. This is simpler than the separate loop the first spec described; the spec is updated.\n\n**Test:** `TestJournalDiffListsRowOnlyChanges` (`engine/working_test.go`) covers:\n- insert-only, update-only and delete-only changes after a checkpoint;\n- empty after a checkpoint;\n- empty after a native-git write;\n- a new table listed as `added` beside a `modified` one;\n- the same result after reopening from disk, with `Status` dirty.\n\nIt failed before the fix.\n\n**CLI checked by hand:** journal-mode server, then `commit`, then an `INSERT`. `repodb status` reports dirty and `repodb diff` prints `modified\tt`.\n\n**Docs:** `cli.md`, `library.md` and `testing.md` no longer cite the limitation and describe the current behavior.\n\n`make test` and `make lint` pass."},"created_at":"2026-10-01T11:20:19.670991Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
