{"id":"rdb-f4dec8","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-25e03d9b-8434-4a17-8211-6911dcded53a","text":"Ready for review.\n\n**Removed:**\n- `experiments/gitstorage` (`make m0`) and `experiments/m2bench` (`make m2-bench`);\n- `storage.Filesystem` and its test;\n- `common/query`;\n- `Repository.CacheDir()` and the `repodb/cache/` doc line;\n- `Writer.PendingHashes()`: unused and named after \"the journal prototype\". It wasn't on the list; I removed it as the same kind of leftover.\n\n**Renamed:**\n- `make m4.2-bench` → `make bench-go`; `make m4.3-bench` → `make bench-journal`.\n- `BenchmarkM43*` → `BenchmarkJournal*`, except `BenchmarkDurableSave`, which runs both modes, so I didn't give it the `Journal` prefix.\n\n**Reworded:** the four milestone error strings, without \"M2\", and the AUTO_INCREMENT/generated-column error now says what's unsupported. Also the `WorkingState`, `CommitTypedEdits` and `Checkpoint` comments. `docs/sql.md` quotes are updated, and no test asserted the old strings.\n\n**Docs:**\n- `architecture.md`: `common/storage` row;\n- `cli.md`: cache line;\n- `sql.md`: error quotes;\n- `testing.md`: storage bullet removed, benchmark table renamed, the two make targets documented.\n\n**Checks:**\n- the acceptance `git grep` is clean (only \"Apple M1 Max\" in the README);\n- `make build`, `make test` and `make lint` pass;\n- all six renamed benchmarks run one iteration."},"created_at":"2026-10-01T12:44:18.647798Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
