{"id":"rdb-c85855","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-63fbf3a1-6566-4185-847f-7cddb009d683","text":"Root cause found: **rdb-fb3d12** (Prolly chunk boundaries weren't content-local), not system fsync stalls. Small edits sometimes rewrote up to half a table's Prolly tree, so `hash-object -w` and `write-tree` had to write and fsync 10–20× more objects in that commit. That's exactly the \"both writers slow together, nothing else slow\" signature recorded here.\n\nNative-git dbbench at 50k rows with the rdb-fb3d12 fix (`run-fb`) vs the three earlier runs (ms, p50/p95/max):\n\n| workload | run1 | run2 | run3 | run-fb |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| update_batch_1 | 203/278/434 | 194/254/435 | 224/375/811 | 153/162/168 |\n| update_batch_10 | 268/1122/1405 | 235/1070/1456 | 290/2021/2906 | 152/158/165 |\n| update_batch_100 | 244/447/476 | 261/449/488 | 254/440/463 | 176/181/183 |\n| insert | 161/174/174 | 160/223/371 | 152/156/158 | 148/154/155 |\n| delete | 161/176/179 | 160/169/174 | 157/165/168 | 150/157/164 |\n\nRequests over 1 s in update_batch_10: 2, 2, 2 before, **0** after.\n\nProposed: close this issue as resolved by rdb-fb3d12 once that merges."},"created_at":"2026-10-01T19:25:44.725614Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-fb3d12","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-256b7802-ce15-4860-b19b-fe586e8d3d78","text":"Ready for review.\n\n**Fix** (`common/prolly/tree.go`). Chunk boundaries are now content-local: a leaf entry's **key** hash or a link's **MaxKey** hash, no accumulation, same 32/128/6-bit options. `chunk()`, `leafChunker` (Apply) and `SortedBuilder` share `shouldCut` / `entryBoundaryHash` / `linkBoundaryHash`, and the rolling state is gone. `repository.FormatVersion` goes 3 → 4: tree shapes change, and alpha needs no migration.\n\n**Tests:**\n- All existing Prolly tests pass unchanged, including `Apply` equals a fresh `Build`.\n- New `TestApplyRewritesOnlyTouchedChunks` (10k entries, depth 3):\n  - updates write ≤ 3 nodes (exactly one per level);\n  - inserts and deletes ≤ 9 (measured over 271 positions: median 3, worst 8);\n  - k adjacent updates ≤ 3k;\n  - every result is checked against a fresh `Build`.\n  - Before the fix, a single-key update wrote 47–106 nodes.\n- `make test` and `make lint` pass, with no fixture pinned to format 3.\n\n**Results:**\n- `BenchmarkJournalCheckpoint` batch=10: ~1,200 → 207–298 ms, now in line with batch=1/100.\n- New objects per checkpoint, k = 1..100: 12–231 → 12–14.\n- `BenchmarkSQLWriteBatches` (native-git): 2–3× faster (mutations=1: 350 → 150 ms; 1000: 650 → 345 ms).\n- Native-git dbbench at 50k rows: the update outliers are gone (update_batch_10 max 2,906 → 165 ms), and sync workloads improved (divergent merge p50 1,896 → 1,713 ms). Details on rdb-c85855, which this resolves.\n\n**Docs:** `architecture.md` (Prolly boundary rule, Apply cost, `RepoDB snapshot v4`) and `testing.md`. `latest.md` waits for the next scorecard."},"created_at":"2026-10-01T19:25:44.755349Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
