{"id":"rdb-c56142","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-2a053050-8335-4e64-967a-193a5ab610bc","text":"Ready for review.\n\n- **Defaults.** `repodb start` and `repodb-server` default to journal; `--persistence native-git` is audit mode. Both print the mode at startup.\n- **Sync.**\n  - `integration.SyncWithOptions` with `SyncOptions.Checkpoint` checkpoints a dirty journal before each attempt, and retries (`working-dirty-retry`) when a journal commit lands during the fetch or the publication, up to 3 attempts.\n  - CLI: `repodb sync --commit -m \u003cmessage\u003e`.\n  - The terminal prompt now uses the same path.\n  - Without a terminal and without the flag, a dirty journal fails with a message naming `--commit -m`.\n- **Backup and switching modes:** documented, and tested with a copied repository plus switching both ways.\n- **Docs:** README, cli, library, architecture, testing.\n\n**Tests:** CLI defaults and sync flags (cmd/repodb, cmd/repodb-server); sync retry and give-up (integration); mode switching and backup copy (engine). Also an end-to-end run with the built binary: a server in default journal mode, writes, `sync --commit -m` pushing while the server runs.\n\n`make test` and `make lint` pass. The issue's scorecard acceptance item waits for the next scorecard refresh."},"created_at":"2026-10-01T19:40:43.533632Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
