{"id":"rdb-13fbd8","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a0","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-01T20:51:48.657929Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-162912","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Stale native-git writers do full Git publication under the lock before failing (contended throughput regression)","description":"Found in the rdb-13fbd8 scorecard run at `f944eee`; bisected to rdb-e0c717 (`4b66f4a`).\n\n## Symptom\n\ndbbench native-git `contended_increment` at 50k rows:\n- 4 clients: 182 → 243 ms p50, 64 % → 75 % rejected;\n- 16 clients: 180 → 863 ms p50, 4 → 1 ops/s, 68 % → 94 % rejected.\n\nBisect probe (1k rows, 16 native-git sessions × 15 increments, rollback after conflict as dbbench does):\n\n| commit | 4 clients | 16 clients |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cfa8eed` (before rdb-e0c717) | 7.6 ops/s, 48 % rejected, p50 86 ms | 7.3 ops/s, 49 %, 87 ms |\n| `4b66f4a` (rdb-e0c717) | 4.6 ops/s, 75 %, 216 ms | **1.4 ops/s, 94 %, 734 ms** |\n| `f944eee` | same as `4b66f4a` | same |\n\n## Cause\n\nSince rdb-e0c717, native-git commits wait on the publication guard (`lockForPublication`: the guard `WorkingState`'s in-process mutex, then `working.lock`, then `publish.lock`). Waiters queue FIFO instead of polling one file lock. A writer whose snapshot is already stale (another client committed while it waited) still does the full publication work under the lock: `hash-object`, `read-tree`, `update-index`, `write-tree` and `commit-tree`, about 45+ ms. Only then does the `update-ref` compare-and-swap reject it. With 16 contenders, each round serializes 15 doomed publications.\n\nBefore, polling the file lock let a client that had just rolled back barge in with a fresh snapshot and win. That's why rejections were ~50 % rather than the lock-step ideal of 1 − 1/clients.\n\n## Fix\n\nIn `Writer.CommitWithOutcomeMessage`, right after the publication lock is held, compare the current data head with the writer's expected head. If it moved, return `ErrConflict` (outcome rejected) before writing any object. A throwaway experiment recovered 1.4 → 5.5 ops/s and p50 734 → 180 ms at 16 clients. Rejections stay at the FIFO lock-step rate (94 %), which is correct optimistic behavior; per-key conflicts and retry are rdb-df092b.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- A stale writer gets `ErrConflict` without writing any Git object (test).\n- The contended probe is within ~1.5× of the pre-rdb-e0c717 throughput at 16 clients.\n- Existing publication-outcome tests (`committed`, `unknown`, `rejected`) still pass.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a8","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-162912","target_id":"rdb-e0c717","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"rdb-162912","target_id":"rdb-13fbd8","kind":"blocks"},{"source_id":"rdb-162912","target_id":"rdb-df092b","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","performance"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T05:22:42.635072Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
