{"id":"rdb-162912","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a0","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-02T05:22:54.813445Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-162912","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-781d2f79-ed89-4a48-858c-e74a7b5e9848","text":"Ready for review.\n\n**Fix** (`Writer.CommitWithOutcomeMessage`). Right after the publication lock is held, if `w.expected` is set and the current head (`Repository.Head`, cheap through the ref-stamp cache) differs, return `ErrConflict` with outcome `rejected` before writing anything. The `update-ref` CAS stays authoritative, and a failed head read falls through to it.\n\n**Test.** `TestStaleWriterIsRejectedBeforeWritingObjects`: `git count-objects -v` is unchanged after a stale commit. It failed before the fix (13 loose objects written).\n\n**Probe** (native-git, 1k rows, sessions × 15 increments, rollback after conflict), ops/s, p50, rejected:\n\n| commit | 4 clients | 16 clients |\n|---|---|---|\n| `cfa8eed` (before rdb-e0c717) | 7.6, 86 ms, 48 % | 7.3, 87 ms, 49 % |\n| `f944eee` | 4.6, 214 ms, 75 % | 1.4, 732 ms, 94 % |\n| this fix (2 runs) | 9.8–10.0, 100 ms, 73–75 % | 9.5–9.7, 99–100 ms, 90 % |\n\nThroughput is now above the pre-regression level; content-local Prolly (rdb-fb3d12) also makes each commit cheaper. The rejected share stays at the FIFO lock-step rate (one winner per round of concurrent attempts), which is correct optimistic behavior. Fewer rejections need per-key conflicts and retry (rdb-df092b).\n\n**Docs:** `architecture.md` (early rejection) and `testing.md` (the new test; also fixed the stale \"cache deletion\" wording left over from rdb-f4dec8). `make test` and `make lint` pass."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T05:25:48.596276Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
