{"id":"rdb-d690aa","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8641b231-f322-4f82-85ef-c5961f6ff059","text":"Ready for review.\n\n**Implementation:**\n- `repository.Durability` (`full`, `normal`, `off`; zero value = normal) with `ParseDurability`.\n- Platform flushes:\n  - `flush_darwin.go`: full = `File.Sync` (`F_FULLFSYNC`); normal = `fcntl(F_BARRIERFSYNC)` with EINTR retry and an `ENOTSUP`/`EINVAL` fallback to a full flush;\n  - `flush_linux.go`: `fdatasync` for both;\n  - `flush_other.go`: `File.Sync` (Windows `FlushFileBuffers`).\n- `OpenWorkingStateWithOptions(repo, WorkingOptions{Durability})`; `groupSync` flushes at the level, and `off` skips it.\n- **Checkpoint rule:** `Checkpoint` and `CheckpointPrepared` call `flushJournalFully()` before `CommitWithOutcomeMessage`. Compaction's temp-file flush is always full.\n- Wiring: `engine.Options.Durability`, `server.Config.Durability`, `--durability` on `repodb start` and `repodb-server` (validated, printed at startup), and dbbench `-durability` with the report's `durability` field (also passed to the reopen subprocess).\n- `repodb-server` now prints flag-validation errors instead of exiting silently.\n\n**Tests:**\n- `durability_internal_test.go`:\n  - per-level flush per commit (`off` → none, zero value → normal);\n  - the checkpoint's first flush is full and happens while the head is unchanged; it fails when the pre-publish flush is removed;\n  - real flush calls succeed on this OS;\n  - `ParseDurability`.\n- engine: `TestJournalCommitsSurviveProcessKill` (subprocess commits 20 rows and gets SIGKILL; all 20 present at every level) and `TestEngineDurabilityOption`.\n- CLI flag tests for both binaries.\n- `make test` (including the Windows cross-build and vet) and `make lint` pass.\n\n**Measured** (single-row autocommit `UPDATE`, 50k rows, macOS, 300 commits each):\n\n| level | p50 | flush part |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| full | 5.01 ms | 4.51 ms |\n| normal | **0.47 ms** | 0.27 ms |\n| off | 0.21 ms | 0 |\n\n**Docs:** architecture (durability table, why nothing corrupts, the checkpoint rule), cli (Persistence modes section, flag tables), library (`Options.Durability`, `RecoverTransaction` caveat, server default), benchmark (the `durability` field), README (commands table, architecture bullet), testing.\n\n**Not changed:** the README performance sentence \"~5 ms (one `fsync`)\" quotes the published 87dd885 scorecard and is replaced by the next scorecard (rdb-d58a06)."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T06:46:35.306763Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
