{"id":"rdb-43dc0e","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"A 71 MB dbbench binary is tracked at the repository root","description":"Found while implementing rdb-d58a06: `go build ./experiments/dbbench` in the repo root overwrote a **tracked** file `dbbench`, a 71 MB Mach-O arm64 executable committed by accident in `e33870e` (rdb-22f505, 2026-09-28).\n\n## Fix (on the rdb-d58a06 branch)\n\n- `git rm dbbench`.\n- Add `/dbbench` to `.gitignore`, next to the existing `dbbench.json` entry, so local builds of the harness don't show up again.\n\n## Not done\n\nThe blob stays in Git history (about 71 MB in every clone). Removing it needs a history rewrite of published commits, which is the owner's call.","status":"DOING","sort_order":"a1","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@MBPM1X.local\u003e","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-43dc0e","target_id":"rdb-d58a06","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"rdb-43dc0e","target_id":"rdb-22f505","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T06:55:34.614934Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-d58a06","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-02T06:59:05.081844Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-d58a06","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-f140a4c1-c733-498f-b911-ec010bc18eed","text":"Ready for review.\n\n**Built:**\n- `experiments/dbbench/Dockerfile`: `golang:1.27-trixie` to build, `debian:trixie-slim` with Git to run, non-root user with a Git identity.\n- `.dockerignore`.\n- `make bench-docker`: clean-tree guard with a `BENCH_ALLOW_DIRTY=1` override; creates the `repodb-bench` network and the `repodb-bench-fixtures` volume, emptying the volume before each run.\n- dbbench `-revision`, `-working-tree-status` and `-runtime` flags; `newReport`; a `runtime` report field.\n\n**Beyond the spec.** The MySQL and Dolt baselines are also measured from inside Docker (`BENCH_MODE=external`, reached by container name on the network). The old host-side harness went through Docker Desktop's port forwarding, which isn't like for like. `docs/benchmark.md` has the full Setup section and commands.\n\n**Bug fixed here: rdb-43dc0e.** A 71 MB macOS `dbbench` binary was tracked at the repo root since `e33870e`. Removed and ignored; the blob remains in history.\n\n**Verified:**\n- dirty-tree refusal;\n- journal smoke in Docker (all PASS; report linux/arm64, go1.27.1, git 2.47.3, `runtime: docker`, `durability: normal`);\n- external smoke against `repodb-bench-mysql:3306` over the network (8.4.11).\n- `make test` and `make lint` pass. The MySQL and Dolt containers are now attached to the `repodb-bench` network."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T06:59:05.111311Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-d58a06","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8eea15d2-ee68-4651-873f-87aad96dcb7a","text":"Scorecard refresh done in this issue (user decision), all four systems in Docker.\n\n**Revision handling.** The harness changes are committed on the branch as `636af3d`, and the scorecard measured that clean commit. latest.md and the README are a second commit. The merge must use **strategy `ff`** (not squash) so `636af3d` stays on main, since the published reports name it.\n\n**Run** (`make bench-docker`, one container at a time, `servaint-*` stopped with the user's OK): native-git 2.4 min, journal 2.5 min, MySQL 5 s, Dolt 7 s. All four reports record `636af3d`, a clean tree, `runtime: docker`, linux/arm64 and Git 2.47.3; RepoDB at `durability: normal`. Dolt failed correctness again. No fixture stopped.\n\n**Results (50k rows, p50):**\n\n| | MySQL | Dolt | Journal |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| point read | 0.04 | 0.14 | 0.07 |\n| range 100 | 0.15 | 0.26 | 0.11 |\n| read tx | 0.94 | 2.1 | 0.71 |\n| full scan | 13 | 20 | 34 |\n| join | 2.6 | 12 | 45 |\n| update x1 | 0.57 | 1.0 | 0.48 |\n| insert | 0.55 | 0.75 | 0.56 |\n| update x100 | 8.4 | 25 | 3.0 |\n\n**Main finding.** The earlier read advantage was mostly host port forwarding (~0.15–0.2 ms per baseline request), and the earlier write gap was the host's `F_FULLFSYNC`. Like for like:\n- MySQL is faster on point reads, scans and joins;\n- RepoDB's journal is on par for single-row writes and ~3× faster for 100-row batches.\n\n**Published:**\n- latest.md: header, environment (VM, images, durability, isolation), make commands, summary, a \"Changes since `87dd885`\" that explains the setup change instead of comparing numbers, and rendered tables.\n- The four JSONs.\n- README: performance section regenerated from the JSON, plus the scope sentence (writes ~0.5 ms, batches ~3 ms, merges ~1 s).\n\nChecks: links resolve, `git diff --check`, `make lint`."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:20:59.557572Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
