{"id":"rdb-48f066","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Speed up full scans and joins (binary Prolly nodes, decoded-node cache, per-row overhead)","description":"## Problem\n\nThe like-for-like scorecard (all systems in Docker, `636af3d`, latest.md) shows RepoDB's weakest spot is now whole-table reads. 50k rows, p50:\n\n| | MySQL 8.4 | Dolt 2.3 | RepoDB journal |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| Full scan (`SELECT * FROM bench`) | 13 ms | 20 ms | 34 ms |\n| Join + aggregate (`SELECT a.name, COUNT(*) FROM bench b JOIN authors a ON a.id = 1 GROUP BY a.name`) | 2.6 ms | 12 ms | 45 ms |\n\nPoint reads, ranges, read transactions and writes are sub-millisecond or close to MySQL, so this is the main read gap.\n\n## Diagnosis (CPU profile of `BenchmarkSQLAutocommitScans/fullscan`, 50k rows, journal, 2026-10-02)\n\n- **About 32 ms per scan, about 25 ms of it CPU in `Session.Query`.** 509k allocations and 29 MB per scan.\n- **About half the CPU is decoding Prolly nodes:** `prolly.readNode` → `encoding/json.Unmarshal` with base64 decoding of every key and value (0.47 of 0.99 s). Nodes are stored as JSON with base64 byte strings. Every scan re-decodes every node, because only raw object bytes are cached, not decoded nodes.\n- **The rest:** `mergedEntries` (the pending-edit overlay merge), row decoding, go-mysql-server's per-row iterator stack (`TransactionCommittingIter` → `ProjectIter`) and allocations/GC.\n- **The join** costs the scan plus per-row join work. `ON a.id = 1` is a constant condition on `authors`: MySQL resolves it as a constant lookup and counts rows, while RepoDB, through go-mysql-server, iterates the join row by row.\n\n## Directions (to spec)\n\n1. **Binary node encoding:** length-prefixed keys and values instead of JSON+base64. Storage format bump (alpha: no migration). Likely the largest single win; it also shrinks objects and checkpoint bytes. Coordinate with rdb-a0d510 (chunk size), which also bumps the format.\n2. **Decoded-node cache:** an LRU of decoded nodes per repository, keyed by content hash. Immutable nodes make this safe. It would make repeated scans and hot subtrees allocation-light.\n3. **Fewer allocations per row:** reuse row buffers in `primaryRowIter`/`mergedEntries`; avoid copying keys and values that go-mysql-server copies anyway; skip the overlay merge when no pending edits exist.\n4. **Join planning:** see whether go-mysql-server can treat a constant-key condition on a primary key as a lookup (statistics, `sql.IndexAddressable` hints), or whether RepoDB's table needs to expose row counts and statistics for the planner.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Full scan and join at 50k rows measured before and after with `make bench-docker` (like for like), and the per-scan CPU profile recorded in the issue.\n- Targets to set in the spec, after a binary-node prototype shows the achievable range; for example full scan ≤ MySQL's, join within 2× of Dolt's.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a8","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-48f066","target_id":"rdb-d58a06","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"rdb-48f066","target_id":"rdb-acd36d","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"rdb-48f066","target_id":"rdb-a0d510","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["feature","performance"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:28:33.90617Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-3e058b","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"README wrongly says Dolt lacks version history and cross-clone sync","description":"README.md (Performance section) says: \"Neither MySQL nor Dolt provides Git-native version history or cross-clone synchronization.\"\n\nThat is false for Dolt. Dolt has Git-style commits, branches, diffs and merges, plus clone/push/pull through remotes. Since v1.81.10 (February 2026) it can also use plain Git remotes, such as GitHub, as Dolt remotes: https://www.dolthub.com/blog/2026-02-13-announcing-git-remote-support-in-dolt/\n\nThe sentence was meant to explain why the sync table has no baselines. The real reason is that the benchmark harness runs sync and merge workloads only against RepoDB (docs/benchmark.md, \"External baselines\").","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a9","labels":["bug","docs"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:33:53.736501Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.287 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
