{"id":"rdb-a6a4d2","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-6de2e3d2-ca48-4b95-8cbe-aede56fd3dca","text":"## Implemented (awaiting review)\n\n**What changed**\n- `common/repository/pending.go`: `PendingRows`, an immutable set of sorted runs, newest first, merged size-tiered (`With`, `Get`, `Iter`, `Len`, `Empty`). Replaces `map[string]TypedRowEdit` in `pendingTableEdits` and `Snapshot.PendingEdits()`. `applyTypedEditsToSnapshot` shares untouched tables and copies only the edited table's small entry struct.\n- Engine `tableState`: `pending` (shared, encoded, decoded on access) plus `edits` (this transaction's own). Helpers: `edit`, `decodePending`, `hasEdits`, `forEachEdit`, `overlayDeletes`. The `decodedEdits` cache and the per-transaction map copy are gone.\n- `commitTypedEdits` writes only `state.edits`. DDL that rewrites a table clears `pending`, since its `edits` already hold every row.\n- Scans: `mergedEntries` takes an `overlayCursor`. `rowOverlayCursor` merges local keys with `PendingRows.Iter` in key order. Secondary-index scans use `keyCursor`, unchanged.\n- Checkpoint iterates `PendingRows` in key order (no sort).\n- Removed the unused `WorkingState.PendingTableEdits` (it returned an unexported type) and the never-set `pendingTableEdits.dropped`.\n- Docs: `architecture.md` (prepare record contents, pending-edit structure).\n\n**Decisions not in the spec**\n- `rekeyRows` receives only the overlay's deletes (`overlayDeletes`), which is all it used. Decoding pending rows there failed because `ModifyColumn` changes the schema before re-keying.\n\n**Measured** (probe, 50k-row table, journal, 200 iterations)\n\n| P | `UPDATE` before → after | Journal bytes/`UPDATE` before → after | Point read before → after |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 0 | 0.40 → 0.38 ms | 419 → 419 B | 87 → 83 µs |\n| 1,000 | 1.12 → 0.38 ms | 86 KB → 419 B | 112 → 74 µs |\n| 10,000 | 6.79 → 0.37 ms | 856 KB → 419 B | 432 → 77 µs |\n\n**Tests:** `TestPendingRowsMatchesModel` (random model, persistence of old versions, run count bound), `TestPendingRowsLastEditInBatchWins`, `TestPendingRowsIterInterval`, `TestJournalCommitAppendsOnlyOwnEdits` (record size with 2,000 pending edits, pending-only delete, replay and checkpoint). `make test` and `make lint` pass.\n\n**Out of scope, filed separately:** secondary-index scans still rebuild and sort the index overlay per query."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:59:30.686038Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-24820a","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Secondary-index scans rebuild and sort the pending index overlay on every query","description":"Found while fixing rdb-a6a4d2, which made primary-key reads and journal commits independent of the number of pending edits (P).\n\nSecondary-index reads still cost O(P_index) per query. `newIndexRowIter` (`engine/ranges.go`) copies `state.idxEdits[def.Name]` into a fresh map on every index scan, and each interval then filters and sorts that map's keys (`sortedOverlayKeys`). The cached index edits (`storeIndexEdits` / `compactIndexEdits`) are already sorted and unique per generation, so only the transaction's own appended edits need sorting.\n\n**Direction:** keep the cached per-generation index edits as a sorted, shared run (or a `PendingRows`-like structure) and merge the transaction's own edits over it in key order, as `rowOverlayCursor` does for rows.\n\n**Acceptance:** an index point lookup with 10,000 pending inserts is within 1.5× of one with none.","status":"BACKLOG","sort_order":"af","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-24820a","target_id":"rdb-a6a4d2","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug","performance"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T07:59:30.7175Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
