{"id":"rdb-48f066","type":"ARTIFACT","payload":{"artifact_type":"spec","filename":"spec.md","action":"updated"},"created_at":"2026-10-02T08:20:45.02248Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-48f066","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-ab80d457-ca41-4adc-b201-74142735d6f2","text":"## Implemented (awaiting review)\n\n**What changed**\n- `common/prolly/codec.go` (new): binary node codec and an in-place `nodeReader`. Links carry subtree counts. `walk`/`Reachable` verify every count. `Tree.Count` reads only the root. The iterator parses leaves in place, and `Get` searches in place.\n- Store contract: `Get` returns shared read-only bytes. `snapshotStore`, `Writer` and `Memory` no longer copy. `Hash.Valid` no longer allocates and still accepts upper- and lowercase hex. Audit: no caller writes into returned bytes (details in the spec's Edge Cases).\n- Format 4 → 5; `snapshotValidationVersion` 1 → 2.\n- Engine:\n  - `sql.ProjectedTable` with `decodeRowProjected`, which skips unneeded cells and stops after the last needed column.\n  - `sql.StatisticsTable`: `RowCount` is exact from the tree count when no edits are pending, otherwise an estimate.\n  - The per-row `encodeKey` check is gone from scans.\n  - `mergedEntries` no longer converts tree keys to strings.\n- Benchmarks: `join` and `count` added to `BenchmarkSQLAutocommitScans`.\n- Docs: `architecture.md` (node encoding, store contract, access paths, format 5, the stale \"currently 3\"), `testing.md`.\n\n**Decisions not in the original spec** (the spec is updated to match)\n- `RowCount`'s estimate adds `len(edits)` without inspecting them, so planning stays O(1).\n- A column projected twice is copied from its first decoded value.\n- `Get` still returns a copy of the value.\n\n**In-process, macOS M1 Max, 50k rows, journal** (`BenchmarkSQLAutocommitScans`, main → branch)\n\n| Case | main | branch |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| range100 | 143 µs | 61 µs |\n| limit20 | 75 µs | 41 µs |\n| range10k | 6.5 ms | 2.3 ms |\n| fullscan | 32.7 ms, 509k allocs | **12.1 ms**, 302k allocs |\n| join | ~35 ms | **12.7 ms** |\n| count | ~28 ms | **27 µs** (`table_count`) |\n\nAll three in-process targets are met.\n\n**Linux container (4 CPUs, Go 1.27):** full scan 32.6 → 13.4 ms, join 16.5 ms, count 34 µs.\n\n**Per-scan CPU profile (Linux).** Main: 3.27 s CPU for 100 scans, of which `prolly.readNode` → `encoding/json.Unmarshal` was 1.85 s (57%). Branch: Prolly iteration is 0.18 s across 300 queries. What's left is `decodeRowProjected` (0.35 s), `mergedEntries` (0.25 s), go-mysql-server's iterator stack (`TrackedRowIter` → `ProjectIter`) and allocation. On macOS, CPU profiles undercount badly (rusage shows about 15 ms of CPU per scan across threads), so I recorded the Linux profiles.\n\n**`make bench-docker BENCH_MODE=journal`** (diagnostic, `BENCH_ALLOW_DIRTY=1`, same Docker VM; p50, before = latest.md at `636af3d`):\n\n| 50k rows | before | after | MySQL | Dolt |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| full_scan | 34.1 ms | **13.4 ms** | 12.9 ms | 20.5 ms |\n| join_aggregate | 45.0 ms | **14.6 ms** | 2.6 ms | 11.8 ms |\n| ordered_limit (DESC) | 39.1 ms | 18.1 ms | 0.06 ms | 0.21 ms |\n| point_read | 0.075 ms | 0.034 ms | 0.037 ms | 0.140 ms |\n| range_read | 0.112 ms | 0.061 ms | 0.151 ms | 0.258 ms |\n| read_transaction | 0.71 ms | 0.26 ms | 0.94 ms | 2.12 ms |\n| publish_sync_after_writes | 306 ms | 219 ms | | |\n\nDocker targets: the join is within 2× of Dolt (1.24×). The full scan is at parity with MySQL rather than below it: 13.4 ms against MySQL's 12.9 ms from the `636af3d` run, a gap smaller than the 1.7× run-to-run swing latest.md reports for MySQL. The descending `ordered_limit` still sorts (rdb-acd36d). Writes are unchanged within noise.\n\n**Tests:** `codec_internal_test.go` (round trip, every truncation, trailing bytes, JSON and unknown-version headers, clipped capacity, wrong child count), `TestCountMatchesEntries`, `TestDecodeRowProjectedMatchesDecodeRow`, `TestProjectedReadsMatchFullRows` (native-git and journal, committed and in-transaction), `TestCountStarUsesRowCount`. `make test` and `make lint` pass.\n\n**Merge note:** rdb-a6a4d2 changes the same overlay code (`mergedEntries`, `tableState.edits`). Whichever merges second needs a small rebase. After a6a4d2, `RowCount` must check `hasEdits()` (pending or local), not just `len(s.edits)`.\n\nlatest.md is not updated here. Publishing a scorecard needs a clean commit of every mode (`docs/benchmark.md`)."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T08:21:07.08786Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
