{"id":"rdb-24820a","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"title":"Secondary-index reads and writes cost O(pending index edits) per statement","description":"Found while fixing rdb-a6a4d2, which made primary-key reads and journal commits independent of the number of pending edits (P). Secondary indexes still pay O(P_index) per statement.\n\nMeasured on `main` at `1178237` (50k rows, `UNIQUE INDEX ue (email)`, `INDEX ig (grp)`, journal, P rows inserted after the last checkpoint):\n\n| P | unique lookup | non-unique lookup | `UPDATE` of an indexed column |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 0 | 48 µs | 127 µs | 0.57 ms |\n| 1,000 | 150 µs | 231 µs | 1.18 ms |\n| 10,000 | 982 µs | 1,163 µs | 5.14 ms |\n\n**Causes** (`state.idxEdits map[string][]prolly.Edit`, an append-only edit list per index):\n1. `newIndexRowIter` copies every edit of the index into a map and sorts its keys, per query.\n2. `lookupIndexKey` (unique checks on insert and update) scans every edit linearly.\n3. `editor.StatementBegin` copies every index edit, to undo a failed statement.\n4. `storeIndexEdits` and `rememberIndexEdits` re-compact and sort every edit, per journal commit.\n\n**Direction:** hold each index's journal edits as a shared `repository.PendingRows` (cached per generation) plus the transaction's own appended edits. Scans and lookups merge the two; statement undo truncates the local edits; a commit caches `base.With(local)`.\n\n**Acceptance:** index lookups and indexed writes at P = 10,000 within 1.5× of P = 0.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"a8","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-02T08:59:50.567177Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
