{"id":"rdb-24820a","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"a0","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-02T08:59:54.196777Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-24820a","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-8fdef81b-6ae0-4aed-bee2-d7f7a0fa997f","text":"## Implemented (awaiting review)\n\n**What changed** (`engine/catalog.go`, `engine/ranges.go`)\n- `indexOverlay{base repository.PendingRows; local []repository.TypedRowEdit}` replaces the per-index `[]prolly.Edit`. Methods: `add`, `get` (local backwards, then `base.Get`), `view` (`base.With(local)`), `sorted`.\n- Cache `database.indexEdits` holds `PendingRows` per index. `StartTransaction` wraps them without copying. `storeIndexEdits` and `rememberIndexEdits` cache `view()`. `compactIndexEdits`, `shareIndexEdits` and `coalesceEdits` are gone.\n- `ensureIndexEdits` turns derived edits into the shared base (once per generation, as before).\n- `lookupIndexKey` uses `get`. `newIndexRowIter` iterates `view()` through a new `pendingCursor`: no map, no sort.\n- Statement undo records local lengths and truncates back to them, instead of copying every edit.\n- Docs: `architecture.md` (pending-edits paragraph), `testing.md`.\n\n**Decision not in the spec:** `DiscardChanges` also drops an overlay that `addIndexEdit` created during the statement. That only happens for an index created earlier in the same transaction, since `ensureIndexEdits` creates one for every existing index.\n\n**Measured** (probe, 50k rows, `UNIQUE (email)` + `INDEX (grp)`, journal, `main` at `1178237` → branch):\n\n| P | unique lookup | non-unique lookup | `INSERT` | indexed `UPDATE` |\n|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|\n| 0 | 51 → 52 µs | 127 → 132 µs | 0.56 → 0.56 ms | 0.51 → 0.45 ms |\n| 1,000 | 149 → 45 µs | 232 → 121 µs | 1.15 → 0.54 ms | 1.12 → 0.46 ms |\n| 10,000 | 1,019 → 44 µs | 1,174 → 110 µs | 5.50 → 0.48 ms | 5.26 → 0.39 ms |\n\n**Tests:** `TestJournalIndexOverlayLayers` covers unique checks against pending-only keys, rollback of a failed multi-row statement's index entries, a local delete hiding a pending-only key, a local update moving a row into the scanned range, commit, and a reopened engine. `make test` and `make lint` pass."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T09:06:42.60478Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
