{"id":"rdb-2945ff","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-5e1a6750-1f98-4abc-beed-035e1968bc09","text":"## Ready for review\n\n- **Measured** all four modes with `make bench-docker` at the clean commit `6b76e87`, run from this issue's worktree before any edit (`working_tree_status` empty in every report). Runs were sequential, with one baseline container at a time, and the unrelated `servaint-*` containers stopped (user approved). The baseline image digests match latest.md (MySQL `0744ee5e…`, Dolt `36fdd43d…`). Docker 29.8.1, kernel 7.0.14-linuxkit, macOS 15.8 on AC power, all unchanged.\n- **Tables** come from a render script, validated first by reproducing the `636af3d` Results section byte for byte from that run's JSON.\n- **\"Changes since `636af3d`\"** uses the MySQL and Dolt reruns as the noise reference: middle-80% ratios of 0.92–1.34× (MySQL) and 0.85–1.14× (Dolt), extremes 0.6–2.4×. Only RepoDB changes well beyond that are claimed.\n- **README:** the performance table (Ordered limit row added), the paragraph, the intro sentence, and the removed \"until reverse index scans land\" sentence.\n- **Dolt** failed correctness again (lost updates and serialization errors under contended increment), so its `make` exit was 2, as in the previous run. It's marked ✗.\n- **Flagged in latest.md, not investigated:** the journal harness's peak RSS rose 276 → 350 MiB (native Git fell 217 → 140). It's a single sample."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T10:03:29.387081Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
