{"id":"rdb-df092b","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-02T12:27:53.582346Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-9afb3c","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"Derived journal index edits drop a unique value that moved to another row","description":"Found while implementing rdb-40ba7c, by its randomized rebase model test. The bug predates that change.\n\n## Symptom\n\nOn a table with a persisted unique index:\n\n```sql\n-- checkpointed: (1, u=10), (2, u=20)\nDELETE FROM t WHERE id = 2;\nUPDATE t SET u = 20 WHERE id = 1;\n```\n\nAn engine that derives index edits from the journal, instead of using the per-generation cache (a fresh process, or a cache miss), finds no row for `u = 20`. It also accepts `INSERT INTO t VALUES (3, 20, …)`, which violates the unique constraint.\n\n## Cause\n\n`tableState.overlayIndexEdits` (rdb-e472aa) walks the pending row edits in primary-key order. For each one it emits a delete of the base row's index key, then a put of the new one. Both rows map to the unique key `20`. Row 1's put is emitted before row 2's delete, and the last edit wins, so the key is deleted.\n\n## Fix\n\nEmit each index's deletes before its puts. In the final state at most one row holds a unique key, so its put must win over a former holder's delete. Non-unique keys contain the primary key and never collide.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- [ ] A regression test with a fresh engine: lookup by the moved value finds the new row, and a duplicate insert is rejected.","status":"PLANNED","sort_order":"aA","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@MBPM1X.local\u003e","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-9afb3c","target_id":"rdb-40ba7c","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T12:37:05.265239Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-9afb3c","type":"UPDATE","payload":{"status":"DOING","sort_order":"aZ","dependencies":null,"labels":null},"created_at":"2026-10-02T12:37:10.192365Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-9afb3c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-096bd527-adc0-44fc-a2c3-ba9e5d8d5074","text":"Fixed on the rdb-40ba7c branch (`rdb-40ba7c-per-key-write-conflict-detection-with-commit`), because that issue's model test depends on it. It will be merged with that branch."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T12:37:10.228037Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-40ba7c","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-debd4d8f-2dc4-44d9-8afa-872fcd3edd21","text":"Implementation is complete and ready for review, on branch `rdb-40ba7c-per-key-write-conflict-detection-with-commit` (uncommitted).\n\n**What changed**\n- `common/repository/writelog.go` (new): `writeLog`, which records per-table schema/touch generations and unique-index claim generations, plus `workingView.writeConflict`. Row-key generations are stored on the pending edits themselves: `TypedRowEdit.generation` is unexported and not journaled, so rows need no second map.\n- `CommitTypedEdits` replaces the generation-equality check with `writeConflict`. The data rebase needed no new code, because edits were already applied to the current view.\n- The log is rebuilt in replay (`materialize`) and reset on checkpoint, base change, untyped `prepare` and `reconcileHead`.\n- `TypedTableEdit.Claims` is a new `omitempty` field. The format stays v3.\n- Engine: `uniqueClaims()` fills the claims. After a rebased commit, `storeIndexEdits` extends the cache of the generation it landed on with the transaction's local index edits.\n- Conflict errors wrap `ErrConflict` and name the table and kind of overlap.\n- Docs: `sql.md` (per-mode conflict rules, a write-skew section with the guard-row workaround), `library.md`, `architecture.md` (new §Write conflicts) and `testing.md`.\n\n**Bug found and fixed: rdb-9afb3c.** The new model test exposed a bug that predates this change. `overlayIndexEdits` dropped a unique value that moved to another row after a checkpoint, in any engine deriving index edits (for example, a fresh process). It also accepted a duplicate insert. The fix emits removals before additions; a serial regression test is in `journal_index_test.go`.\n\n**Tests**\n- `writelog_internal_test.go`: a 14-case conflict matrix, rebase across generations and processes, coverage rules, and faults (before append, after flush, torn tail).\n- `journal_rebase_test.go`: SQL-level disjoint, same-row, unique/NULL, DDL, checkpoint and cross-engine cases, plus a randomized model test (60 rounds × 3 transactions, one or two engines). The model test passed 40 seeds.\n- Four existing tests used disjoint stale writers. Their stale writer now writes the same row, so they still test rejection.\n- Mutation-checked: a stale index cache and missing claims each make the new tests fail.\n- `go test ./...`, `go vet`, `-race` on repository/engine/integration, and a `GOOS=windows` build all pass.\n\n**dbbench (journal, 50k rows, 100 requests/client; macOS host, a single run each)**\n\n| | main | branch |\n|---|---|---|\n| mixed, 4 clients: conflicts | 29 | **0** |\n| mixed, 16 clients: conflicts | 189 | **0** |\n| mixed, 16 clients: successful writes / wall | 131 / 68 ms | 320 / 110 ms |\n| contended_increment, 16 clients | 1273 conflicts, lost-update check ✓ | 1263 conflicts, lost-update check ✓ |\n\nMixed ops/s and p50 look worse on the branch because rejections used to fail fast without a flush. Now every write appends and flushes, so successful writes per second rose from about 1.9k to about 2.9k, while wall time grew. Other workloads are within noise."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:02:00.540527Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
