{"id":"rdb-f8b841","type":"CREATE","payload":{"title":"make lint fails: SA4000 identical expressions in dbbench TestFixturesAreDeterministic","description":"Found while running `make lint` for rdb-2c93ca. The failure is already on `main` (introduced in d0e30db, rdb-db5459).\n\n`experiments/dbbench/workloads_test.go:32` compares `commentBody(7) != commentBody(7)` directly, and staticcheck flags it as SA4000 (identical expressions on both sides of `!=`). `make lint` fails.\n\nFix: call the function into two variables and compare those. The determinism check stays the same.","status":"DOING","sort_order":"a1","assignee":"Claude Code \u003cagent@MBPM1X.local\u003e","dependencies":[{"source_id":"rdb-f8b841","target_id":"rdb-2c93ca","kind":"relates_to"},{"source_id":"rdb-f8b841","target_id":"rdb-db5459","kind":"relates_to"}],"labels":["bug"]},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:47:46.847575Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-2c93ca","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-dfc72b3d-1045-4f93-a3ab-278b0176365f","text":"Implementation done on the branch and uncommitted, waiting for review.\n\n**Git processes RepoDB starts itself** (probe, journal mode, 50k rows; before → after)\n\n| sync | procs | wall (one run, noisy) |\n|---|---|---|\n| up-to-date | 26 → **10** | 397 → 274–368 ms |\n| push `--commit` | 51 → 24 | 818 → 566–606 ms |\n| fast-forward pull | 26 → **17** | 422 → 371–415 ms |\n| merge `--commit` | 72 → **34** | 1128 → 776–985 ms |\n| conflict | 60 → 25 | 850 → 564–596 ms |\n\n**`make bench-sync`-style benchmarks** (`git-procs/op`, `-benchtime=1x`)\n\n| benchmark | procs | time |\n|---|---|---|\n| UpToDateWarm | 16 → 7 | 125 → 74 ms |\n| Divergent sparse-* | 39 → 22 | sparse-50000: 4.74 → 4.06 s |\n| conflict-resolution | 72 → 32 | 619 → 327 ms |\n| rejected-push-retry | 46 → 27 | |\n\n**Changes**\n- `common/git/reader.go`: a long-lived `cat-file --batch` per worktree root.\n  - It serves `ReadObjects`, `ReadTreeFile` (manifest, cache misses) and the new `HasCommit`.\n  - Lifecycle: a 5 s idle close, `CloseReaders`/`CloseAllReaders`, and `engine.Close` calls `CloseReaders`.\n  - Errors and cancellation kill the process. A read that finds an idle process dead retries once.\n- `common/repository/snapshotmemo.go`: a weak memo `(identity, commit) → *snapshotCore`.\n  - `loadSnapshot` and `Writer.Commit` register entries.\n  - Every caller gets a fresh `Snapshot`.\n- `Discover`: one `rev-parse` instead of 3. `OpenWithSnapshot` resolves through `Head()`, so the head cache is primed.\n- Sync:\n  - one `merge-base --all` instead of `--is-ancestor` ×2 plus `merge-base`;\n  - `SnapshotCommit` for commits already resolved;\n  - `fetch()` skips `git fetch` when the tracking ref equals the `ls-remote` head and the commit is present;\n  - after a push, `RemoteHead` is the pushed commit, with no re-fetch.\n- Docs: `architecture.md` (packages, state table, snapshots, sync) and `cli.md` (sync step 1).\n- Tests:\n  - reader: reuse, missing object, objects written later, kill/restart, cancel mid-read, idle and explicit close;\n  - memo: reuse with 0 processes, independent copies, weak collection, committed-snapshot reuse;\n  - sync: tracking ref after a push, no fetch on push or up-to-date, fetch once when the remote moved.\n- `make test` (including the Windows build and vet) and `make lint` pass.\n\n**Deviations from the spec**\n- The fast-forward pull is at **17**, against a target of 16. The extra process is `fetch()`'s pre-check `rev-parse` of the tracking ref; it only costs one when the remote moved. Resolving refs through the long-lived `cat-file` would remove it, but a stale answer there would make sync wrongly skip a fetch, so I didn't.\n- No explicit `update-ref` after a push: verified that `git push \u003ccommit\u003e:refs/repodb/data` updates the tracking ref through the configured fetch refspec. The new sync test asserts it.\n- Readers are keyed by worktree root (the directory Git runs in), not common dir. `CloseReaders(root)` takes `repo.Root`.\n- Also fixed rdb-f8b841, a pre-existing `make lint` failure (SA4000 in dbbench tests from rdb-db5459) that blocked this issue's lint check."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:49:02.112049Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
{"id":"rdb-f8b841","type":"COMMENT","payload":{"id":"cmt-7a34ae1a-51d1-4a5c-b9e8-f54d30827abd","text":"Fixed on the rdb-2c93ca branch (`experiments/dbbench/workloads_test.go`), because that issue's `make lint` check depends on it. It will be merged with that branch."},"created_at":"2026-10-02T13:49:02.142912Z","created_by":"claude-code/2.1.286 \u003cagent@mcp\u003e","on_behalf_of":"Nicolas Bettenburg \u003cnicbet@gmail.com\u003e","source":"mcp"}
